      "text": "SITUATION NOW\nTrials over the assassination of Haiti’s president are resuming in Miami. [1]\nHaiti and Angola are strengthening their cooperation. [2]\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR HAITI\nThe resumption of trials in Miami over the assassination of Haiti’s president occurs while Haiti is linked to 21 US OFAC and Canada SEMA sanctions designations, underscoring the international legal and financial dimensions of the case. [1][E2]\n\nKEY RISKS\nThe Do Not Travel advisory for Haiti signals a high-risk security environment that could deter foreign investment and diplomatic engagement. [E1]\nThe 21 US OFAC and Canada SEMA sanctions designations linked to Haiti create risks of financial isolation and restricted access to international banking systems. [E2]\n\nWATCH ITEMS\nThe outcome of the trials over the assassination of Haiti’s president resuming in Miami remains unresolved. [1]",
